    "question": {
      ":question/id": "e16ec426-4912-5cce-8c0c-6e1e5106e1ac",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix and \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)={\\begin{bmatrix}4{x}_{1} \\\\ -4{x}_{2} \\\\ 0 \\\\ -{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R}?\n$$\n- **I.** $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=0$\n- **II.** $A$ is  invertible\n- **III.** $\\text{Col}(A)\\ne {R}^{5}$\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Since $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,\u21d4\\,{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{5} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=5=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)={0} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Since \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)={{x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R}\n$$\n\nwe conclude that \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))=2\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0,$ then according to the invertible matrix theorem, the matrix $A$ can't be invertible.\n\n- Statement III is true. Since $A$ is not invertible, then by the invertible matrix theorem, we must have $\\text{Col}(A)\\ne {R}^{5}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
